      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14056/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring condensed soup, sugar, vinegar, and oil to a boil in a saucepan. Stir well, remove from the heat, and let cool until needed.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Eah1Np-ikQkcscs-YVfXo_w_Tsw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14056-copper-pennies-ddmfs-step2-3x4-6008-18cc7df1f88c4eba9d52d134f7179d7e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14056/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the same time, bring a large pot of water to a boil; add carrots and boil until just tender, about 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/fBnyB0rB86lZGQGSzVIbxCPqJPI=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/14056-copper-pennies-ddmfs-step3-3x4-6010-927cc2bda2a54ac98095ca288c62c653.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/14056/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain carrots and transfer to a mixing bowl. Add onion, bell pepper, and celery. Pour soup mixture over vegetables and stir until coated. Cover and refrigerate, 8 hours to overnight, before serving.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
